GAMS 54.4.0  9a60ae27 Sep 9, 2026           DAX-DAC arm 64bit/macOS - 10/02/26 17:12:33 Page 1
G e n e r a l   A l g e b r a i c   M o d e l i n g   S y s t e m
C o m p i l a t i o n


      Hay Grain Problem
   4   
   5  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
   6  SETS crop crops growing /Hay, Grain/
   7       res resources /June, July, August, Land/;
   8   
   9  * 2. DEFINE input data
  10  PARAMETERS
  11     c(crop) Objective function coefficients ($ per plant)
  12           /Hay 100,
  13           Grain 120/
  14     b(res) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  15            /June 14000,
  16             July  18000,
  17             August 6000,
  18             Land 10000/;
  19   
  20  TABLE A(crop,res) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  21                   June    July  August Land
  22   Hay             2       1     1      1
  23   Grain           1       2     0      1;
  24   
  25  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  26  VARIABLES X(crop) plants planted (Number)
  27            VPROFIT  total profit ($)
  28            Y(res)  value of resources used (units specific to variable)
  29            VREDCOST total reduced cost ($);
  30   
  31  * Non-negativity constraints
  32  POSITIVE VARIABLES X,Y;
  33   
  34  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  35  EQUATIONS
  36     PROFIT_PRIMAL Total profit ($) and objective function value
  37     RES_CONS_PRIMAL(res) Resource constraints
  38     REDCOST_DUAL Reduced Cost ($) associated with using resources
  39     RES_CONS_DUAL(crop) Profit levels ;
  40   
  41  *Primal Equations
  42  PROFIT_PRIMAL..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(crop,c(crop)*X(crop));
  43  RES_CONS_PRIMAL(res) ..    SUM(crop,A(crop,res)*X(crop)) =L= b(res);
  44   
  45   
  46  *Dual Equations
  47  REDCOST_DUAL..                 VREDCOST =E= SUM(res,b(res)*Y(res));
  48  RES_CONS_DUAL(crop)..          sum(res,A(crop,res)*Y(res)) =G= c(crop);
  49   
  50  X.LO(crop) = 5;
  51   
  52  * 5. DEFINE the MODELS
  53  *PRIMAL model
  54  MODEL PLANT_PRIMAL /PROFIT_PRIMAL, RES_CONS_PRIMAL/;
  55  *Set the options file to print out range of basis information
  56  PLANT_PRIMAL.optfile = 1;
  57   
  58  *DUAL model
  59  MODEL PLANT_DUAL /REDCOST_DUAL, RES_CONS_DUAL/;
  60   
  61  * 6. SOLVE the MODELS
  62  * Solve the PLANTING PRIMAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  63  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  64  SOLVE PLANT_PRIMAL USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  65   
  66  * Solve the PLANTING DUAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  67  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  68  SOLVE PLANT_DUAL USING LP MINIMIZING VREDCOST;
  69  *Order does not matter!
  70   
  71  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file
  72   
  73  * 7 . Dump all data and results to GAMS proprietary file storage .gdx and to Excel
  74  Execute_Unload "ExHW2Dual.gdx";
  75  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
  76  Execute "gdx2xls ExHW2Dual.gdx"
  77  * To open the GDX file in the GAMS IDE, select File => Open.
  78  * In the Open window, set Filetype to .gdx and select the file.


